id: pm-lint-incremental-invalidation
title: Preserve complete lint results with incremental rule invalidation
description: "Retain rule dependency metadata and SDK event cursors to update a complete lint result after unrelated edits. Overlap recheck: existing lint --since filters items by updated_at and drops other findings; lint baselines acknowledge findings without skipping evaluation; portable rule packs and repair previews do not maintain an incremental result. Core listMutationEvents supplies pagination and listAllComplete/certifyCompleteListResult supplies complete corpus certification. Sibling pm-observer cursors track evidence ingestion and pm-graph refreshes graph projections; neither owns lint rule/item dependency invalidation."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-27T08:23:52.579Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-27T09:17:44.490Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "One title edit in 10000 items reruns only affected rules plus declared global checks; the complete result equals a fresh full scan; cursor loss or rule-version drift forces an explicit rebuild; typed SDK and CLI, compact TOON/JSON, typed refusals, README and example, public non-git tracker validation, seeded state properties and interleaving coverage, npm and Bun CI release gates."
parent: pm-lint-epic
comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-27T08:31:39.266Z",codex-agent,"Implemented an SDK-injected incremental engine and a fenced file adapter. Checkpoints keep native-source digests, declared per-rule input digests, violation bits and an SDK cursor anchor; findings are freshly rendered from a certified full read. Global checks are clock, hierarchy, blocker references and SDK duplicates. Core leases serialize checkpoint reads and publication; every source revision and policy is read back through the SDK before publishing. No item mutations or journaled item plans are introduced. Registry version lookup reports 2026.10.27; the repository SDK pin remains 2026.10.23 as required."
  "2026-10-27T08:55:08.856Z",codex-agent,"Read-only public origin/main tracker validation: 21 items, zero findings, source digest 16b7a56ee139b2681ce3ece7e468d9caea102b1cd32a38f9aee4ee638ffaa7d1; authoritative names and bytes preserved. No-op: 12 global predicates, 54 reused pairs. One title edit on a separate disposable derivative: 15 evaluated, 51 reused; result equals fresh full scan. Observed milliseconds: rebuild 3650, no-op 694, edit 288, fresh full 98; incremental reduces predicate work, not every wall-time cost. Seed 0x1ace2026 passed 500 native-state/checkpoint sequences and the second property passed 500 random custom registries. Schema, fenced publication, real 1000-event pagination and all interleaving tests pass. Rule version advances to 2 for lifecycle-role semantics; old baseline documents remain readable and stale acknowledgments are explicit."
  "2026-10-27T09:01:28.248Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: replacing only the incremental evaluator cache decision with false makes the focused equality/reuse regression fail (PML001 evaluated 2 instead of 1; reused 0 instead of 1). Restored the function immediately. Focused coverage run: 36 tests passed, zero failures; all five incremental modules, status adapter and rule predicates reached 100 percent statements/branches/functions/lines in that measured scope. Full package coverage and packed npm/Bun consumer gates remain CI evidence. The registered pm test run executes the nine real incremental regressions on non-git trackers."
  "2026-10-27T09:04:46.797Z",codex-agent,"Registered pm regression run passed all nine incremental tests with no failure categories. The focused measured source set has four incremental implementation modules plus the status adapter at 100 percent in every coverage dimension; the full CI gate supplies package-wide counts and thresholds. Read-only cache evaluation performs no native create/update/import/sync, so ambient create scope, revision-bound idempotency keys and journaled item plans are not introduced. Core events, complete-list certification, lifecycle registry, duplication analysis, leases and atomic publication are reused."
  "2026-10-27T09:17:35.610Z",codex-agent,"PR ready for review: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-lint/pull/32 . CI release gate: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-lint/actions/runs/40479011342 (queued at recording time; PR checks carry the current-head continuation). Compatibility check of the published 2026.10.20 SDK declarations confirms acquireLockLease is absent from its public runtime, index and lock declarations. Raise peer and manifest host minimum to the already pinned/tested 2026.10.23; keep the development SDK pin unchanged. Implementation and targeted acceptance are complete; CI runner scheduling remains external verification. Item stays in progress for orchestrator verification and closure."
